{
  "id": "COMPOUND:28227 - PROTEIN:5944",
  "verbalization": "Tamulamide B is shown to have a target relationship with Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8 through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Tamulamide B acts on two distinct molecular targets: VMRC-LCP and MIP, both of which are involved in the pathway leading to Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8. The first pathway involves a complex compound, (1S,3R,6S,8R,11S,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol, which is a known target of Tamulamide B and ultimately leads to the activation of Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8. The second pathway involves MIP, which is also a target of Tamulamide B and similarly leads to the activation of the same kinase. The third pathway involves Anolobine, another compound that is a target of Tamulamide B and also leads to the activation of Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8. These findings suggest that Tamulamide B may exert its effects through a shared mechanism involving the activation of the Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8 pathway, potentially through the modulation of downstream signaling cascades. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Tamulamide B and the kinase, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
